{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "git.workspaceBranchPlan plans a checkout or a new branch chosen on a common branch across every repository of a workspace, as IntelliJ IDEA's GitBranchOperation runs it: steps run in request order and stop at the first failure; undoing the steps that already ran runs each step's rollback, the last step first. A checkout skips the repositories already on the local branch. Undoing a checkout checks the previous local branch out again, and a remote branch checkout keeps the local branch it created or moved; undoing a new branch checks the previous branch out again when the action switched to it, then deletes the new branch. A step whose repository was detached or unborn before it switched HEAD has rollback null.",
